# Marketing Compliance Checker

This project evaluates financial marketing copy against EU MiFID II regulations.

## How to run a compliance check

When the user asks to evaluate, check, or review marketing copy:

```bash
# From a file
uv run scripts/check_compliance.py --file <path-to-file>

# From inline text
uv run scripts/check_compliance.py --text "<marketing copy>"
```

The script requires `OPENAI_API_KEY` (set via `.env`, environment variable, or `--api-key`).

Use `--file` for multi-line copy. Use `--text` for short single-line input.

The output is JSON with: `overall_verdict` (PASS/FAIL/REVIEW_REQUIRED), `summary`, and per-rule `results`.

## How to re-extract rules

When the user asks to extract or regenerate rules from regulatory sources:

```bash
uv run scripts/extract_rules.py
```

This reads `data/raw_sources/*.md` and writes `data/processed/rules.json`.

## Project structure

- `scripts/check_compliance.py` — CLI entry point for evaluation
- `scripts/extract_rules.py` — CLI entry point for rule extraction
- `src/extractor/` — rule extraction pipeline (prompts, models, pipeline)
- `src/evaluator/` — compliance evaluation pipeline (prompts, models, evaluator, pipeline)
- `src/models.py` — shared Pydantic models (MarketingRule, EvaluationScope)
- `src/llm_client.py` — OpenAI wrapper
- `data/processed/rules.json` — pre-extracted rules (32 rules)
